<div class="hero hero-sm">
  <div>
    <h1>{{page.title}}</h1>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="wrapper">
  <section>
    {{! Every line reads the same whether or not the address has an account,
        so the page tells a stranger nothing (anti-enumeration). The address
        shown is the visitor's own input, never a lookup result, and the
        "may not have an account" hint is shown to everyone for that reason. }}
    <p>
      If an account exists for <strong>{{content.email}}</strong>, we have sent it
      an email with a link to reset your password. Open that email and click the
      link to choose a new password.
    </p>

    <p>
      The link expires in one hour and works once. If the email has not arrived
      within a few minutes, check your spam or junk folder.
    </p>

    <p>
      Still nothing? You may not have an account under that address, or you may
      have used a different one. <a href="/password/forgot">Try another address</a>,
      or <a href="/register">create an account</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      <a href="/login">Return to login</a>
    </p>

    {{#if content.emailPreview}}
      {{> simulated-email-card content.emailPreview emptyHint="No reset email was sent to this address. That happens when no account uses it, or after several requests within an hour. Try another address, or create an account."}}
    {{/if}}
  </section>
</div>
